{"$schema":"https://json.schemastore.org/sarif-2.1.0.json","runs":[{"artifacts":[{"contents":{"text":"<scxml xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2005/07/scxml\" version=\"1.0\" datamodel=\"xpath\" initial=\"a\">\n  <datamodel>\n    <data id=\"count\" expr=\"0\"/>\n    <data id=\"done\" expr=\"false()\"/>\n    <data id=\"user\"><name xmlns=\"\">bob</name></data>\n  </datamodel>\n  <state id=\"a\">\n    <transition event=\"go\" cond=\"true\" target=\"b\"/>\n  </state>\n  <final id=\"b\"/>\n</scxml>\n"},"location":{"uri":"tests/ui/lint011-xpath-bare-true.scx"},"mimeType":"application/scxml+xml"}],"columnKind":"utf16CodeUnits","properties":{"diagnosticCounts":{"errors":0,"notes":0,"total":1,"warnings":1},"producer":{"kind":"validator"}},"results":[{"fixes":[{"artifactChanges":[{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/lint011-xpath-bare-true.scx"},"replacements":[{"deletedRegion":{"byteLength":4,"byteOffset":293,"endColumn":38,"endLine":8,"startColumn":34,"startLine":8},"insertedContent":{"text":"true()"}}]}],"description":{"text":"use `true()`"},"properties":{"applicability":"maybe-incorrect"}}],"level":"warning","locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/lint011-xpath-bare-true.scx"},"region":{"endColumn":38,"endLine":8,"startColumn":34,"startLine":8}}}],"message":{"markdown":"`true` selects a child element named `true`, not the boolean `true()`\n\n**Note:** the context node of every XPath expression is `<datamodel>`, whose children are `<data id=\"…\">` elements and the system variables; an empty node-set is false, so this condition never holds\n\n**Help:** XPath writes the boolean constants as function calls: `true()`\n\n**Spec:** SCXML CR 2014 §C.3.1 Data Model\n\n**Spec:** SCXML CR 2014 §C.3.3 Location Expressions","text":"`true` selects a child element named `true`, not the boolean `true()`"},"properties":{"byteSpan":{"end":297,"start":293},"category":"lint"},"ruleId":"LINT011"}],"tool":{"driver":{"informationUri":"https://www.w3.org/TR/scxml/","name":"scxml-validator","rules":[{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"the context node of every XPath expression is `<datamodel>`, whose children are the `<data id=\"…\">` elements and the system variables, so a bare name such as `count`, `true`, or `_event.data.ok` is a path to a child element with that exact name and selects nothing: a location that selects nothing raises `error.execution`, and a condition is false. In a machine with a `<foreach>`, whose item binds an element of any name, only a declared variable name, `true`/`false`, and a dotted member access are reported"},"help":{"text":"How to fix: reference the variable as `$count`, call `true()`/`false()`, or select a child with a path such as `$_event/data/ok`.\n\nSpecification: SCXML CR 2014 §C.3.1 Data Model\n\nRun `scx --explain LINT011` for examples."},"helpUri":"https://www.w3.org/TR/2014/CR-scxml-20140313/#xpath-datamodel","id":"LINT011","name":"LINT011","properties":{"category":"lint"},"shortDescription":{"text":"an XPath expression starts with a relative path that selects no data"}}],"semanticVersion":"0.2.0"}}}],"version":"2.1.0"}